<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Archibald V. Arnold</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1889">1889</a>–<a href="/years/1973">1973</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Archibald Arnold</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Archibald V. Arnold was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army general who commanded the 7th Infantry Division in the Pacific in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, including in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okinawa">Battle of Okinawa</a>. In September 1945 he became the first military governor of the United States Army Military Government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, south of the 38th parallel. He held the post until early 1946, when he was succeeded by Archer L. Lerch.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/archibald-v-arnold.jpg" alt="Archibald V. Arnold" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown military photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Archibald_Vincent_Arnold.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
